    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1588063774529_247867_88689" xmi:uuid="28087c21-8f90-4b47-ba5f-b4fe4a3103d6" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1588664685799_710512_87350" xmi:uuid="f8b77f74-d90a-4d09-a40e-82f23b3f7c50" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1588063774529_247867_88689"/>
        <body>A BoundedCurveWithLength is a type of BoundedCurve that is not bounded to specified coordinate values but is constrained to a specific CurveLength. The parametrisation of a BoundedCurveWithLength is defined by the distance from the start point, ranging from 0 to CurveLength. &lt;note&gt;A particular point on the BoundedCurveWithLength can be identified with PointOnCurve for a given parameter value that is in the ranges from 0 to CurveLength. &lt;/note&gt;</body>
