    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1533224515214_314437_99004" xmi:uuid="7137c850-6798-4767-8533-5a2ca74fb991" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <name>GeometricSetSelect</name>
      <isAbstract>true</isAbstract>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1533560014622_143593_77001" xmi:uuid="dfb5a108-b2fe-4263-8669-231ad8d344a9" xmi:type="uml:Port">
        <name>geometricSetSelect</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_SYSML_ARM-geometric_set_select"/>
        <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
      </ownedAttribute>
    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1533118799625_363757_94884" xmi:uuid="72089c24-2127-4c33-a36f-21dbc8e6c056" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1536243172778_457741_93578" xmi:uuid="322f6877-e566-4a2d-8515-78b2d6277cb7" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1533118799625_363757_94884"/>
        <body>A Curve11 is a type of DetailedGeometricModelItem that specifies the orientation angle, commonly known as a Rosette, relative to a curve (see Figure below). This method of Rosette representation is suitable for curved parts or tubular part types where it is desired for the primary fiber orientation to follow the path of a curved surface.&lt;br&gt; The following geometric construction method specifies the construction of the Rosette: &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;1.Translate/Transfer the Z Rosette Axis by creating a line normal to the surface at the seed point. Then, transfer the Y Rosette Axis by creating a line through the seed point tangent to the guide curve to produce the transferred X. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;2.Then create a plane through two lines by selecting the normal line first, then by select the transferred X direction vector second. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;3.The normal of this plane should be the cross product of the vector directions for the two lines. The order of selection is important and is done by creating a line normal to the new plane at the seed point. This creates the transferred Y direction. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;4.Transfer the X Rosette Axis by creating a plane through two lines by selecting the transferred Y line first and then select the normal line second. The normal of this plane should be the cross product of the vector directions for the two lines. The order of selection is important. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;5.Finally, create a line normal to this plane at the seed point producing the transferred X direction and then the Fiber11Offset is added to specify the final fiber 11 direction. &lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;Curve_11.gif&lt;/name&gt;Curve11&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>Curve11</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1533199537350_317009_97570" xmi:uuid="a0a3eb0e-45e0-4baf-83ca-0b647b551bc1" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1533199424732_629000_97522"/>
      </generalization>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1533118825749_425971_94929" xmi:uuid="ffc8be07-f60e-4334-810d-4e1a04d60790" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general href="../RepresentationAndExternalElementReference/RepresentationAndExternalElementReference.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193072_543741_23516"/>
      </generalization>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1533119014364_867552_94931" xmi:uuid="3a932b80-76f7-4e37-9b54-5690d55f6a11" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1536243501968_476010_93579" xmi:uuid="e387a9f4-54d0-42bc-9b00-e2e562608bc3" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1533119014364_867552_94931"/>
          <body> the curve specifying the 11 or primary fiber direction. A Curve11 is a Curve that is referenced by the ReinforcementOrientationBasis of a PlyOrientationAngle. There shall exist one or many Curve for a Curve11. </body>
