    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193183_803657_23743" xmi:uuid="7908b19b-2555-41ce-9bcc-3b138fc8be24" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454499867189_430617_43266" xmi:uuid="37d69a6b-ccbd-4c5e-af3b-f5ce7b0fc16b" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193183_803657_23743"/>
        <body>A PlyOrientationAngle is an entity that defines a specific direction within a Ply. The direction is defined in the coordinate axis of a ReinforcementOrientationBasis. The measurement is in degrees between -90 and +90. A PlyOrientationAngle may be one either a DrapedOrientationAngle or a LaidOrientationAngle. &lt;note&gt; For materials with multiple fiber orientations, the direction shall correspond to the warp direction of the material. Warp fibers are the primary load carrying fibers within a fabric material. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; In the design of a specific composite part, a finite set of PlyOrientationAngle values are established for use. An example of a set of commonly used PlyOrientationAngle is (0, 90, +45, -45).&lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>PlyOrientationAngle</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1536311001692_593519_96466" xmi:uuid="b9114497-c5b2-4fbb-833f-e42d0c06be1d" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general href="../RepresentationAndExternalElementReference/RepresentationAndExternalElementReference.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193223_840602_23811"/>
      </generalization>
      <isAbstract>true</isAbstract>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_2aed05bf_1508946851614_104314_38210" xmi:uuid="5f8fcc00-ad23-4aef-9323-02aa979aa533" xmi:type="uml:Port">
        <name>plyOrientationAngle</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_SYSML_ARM-Ply_orientation_angle"/>
