    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193302_777269_23940" xmi:uuid="92a5047c-adf0-4026-9e7e-2e6609a75ba0" xmi:type="uml:Enumeration">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456300029289_688376_42934" xmi:uuid="e18a42ed-469c-4fcd-9355-f52d392f36bb" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193302_777269_23940"/>
        <body>A StockCategoryEnum is an enumeration of StockMaterial type.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>StockCategoryEnum</name>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_2aed05bf_1515592188757_184982_129234" xmi:uuid="ee47a13f-3216-4359-a88b-cb6b847e4fd7" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <name>arm_mapping</name>
        <visibility>private</visibility>
        <type href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_SYSML_ARM-product_shape_type_enumeration"/>
        <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
      </ownedAttribute>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_591974_29433" xmi:uuid="6bde5326-c297-4e44-9092-97f73af25971" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456300044416_303030_42935" xmi:uuid="d38f6bc8-642e-4b18-91c8-96212c533f46" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_591974_29433"/>
          <body> a anisotropic_material is a type of StockMaterial whose properties are different in each material direction.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>anisotropic_material</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_193542_29434" xmi:uuid="3d187135-103a-4c90-a870-02805cf7b0f4" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456300110369_858871_42936" xmi:uuid="bf579c92-0783-4ffa-877e-c2db95a73e28" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_193542_29434"/>
          <body> a braided_assembly is a type of StockMaterial.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>braided_assembly</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_243919_29435" xmi:uuid="57018b34-7125-47b0-94ef-eb44e1488d17" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456300164745_385953_42937" xmi:uuid="32e8e6e8-7956-4146-a43f-89dd8cadd79f" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_243919_29435"/>
          <body> a discontinuous_fiber_assembly is a type of StockMaterial that is a collection of discontinuous fibers suspended in a homogeneous material (matrix). In general, the length of the fibers are relatively the same within a detail. The orientation of the fibers is usually random. &lt;note&gt; When a ply is made from a discontinuous_fiber_assembly, the discontinuous_fiber_assembly is in the form of a sheet or is applied as a constant thickness coating to the area defined by the ply. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; Some resin transfer molded (RTM) parts, where the mixture of short fibers and matrix is injected into a mold, can be viewed as a discontinuous_fiber_assembly. &lt;/note&gt; &lt;example&gt;Fiberglass chop and mat are types of Discontinuous_fiber_assembly (see next figure).&lt;/example&gt; &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;DiscontinuousFiberAssembly.png&lt;/name&gt;Discontinuous fiber assembly&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>discontinuous_fiber_assembly</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_731965_29436" xmi:uuid="28673b63-9f77-448e-91c5-4a2a57138050" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456300209820_984857_42938" xmi:uuid="10269d2b-6ab4-44bb-b8a4-dda4a0c43f1e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_731965_29436"/>
          <body> a filament_assembly is a type of StockMaterial that is a collection of yarns or tows combined together in some manner and frequently embedded in a matrix of homogenous material. The filament_assembly is usually measured by weight and sometimes length to describe the amount needed for a FilamentLaminate. &lt;note&gt; When a ply is made from a filament_assembly it is usually referred to as woven or non-woven fabric such as broad goods and tape. A ply can also be made from such things as a collection of tows or yarn provided the tow or yarn lay flat in the area described by the ply and they are a single thickness that does not stack on top of one another or overlap. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The thickness or cross-sectional area of a filament_assembly is specified in the ply or FilamentLaminate that is made from the stock material. These are usually specified in cured thickness or cross-sectional area. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; Woven and non-woven fabric, individual tows, yarns, and roving are types of filament assemblies (see next figure). &lt;/example&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;FilamentAssembly.png&lt;/name&gt;Filament assembly&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>filament_assembly</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_746513_29437" xmi:uuid="db43f0c0-bedd-45c6-95cb-ade4cfe1d9d3" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456300361187_679063_42939" xmi:uuid="5b2964b0-e81c-4472-8d54-d47631adcaaa" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_746513_29437"/>
          <body> a isotropic_material is a type of StockMaterial that is made up of a single uniform internal structure. &lt;note&gt; When isotropic_material such as resin plays the role of a matrix within other stock materials, the isotropic_material is combined with filaments to make filament assemblies and with fibers to make discontinuous fiber assemblies. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; When isotropic_material such as stabilizers, foaming and film adhesives are applied separately from other stock materials, a ply references the isotropic_material to provide placement and thickness. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; When isotropic_material are such things as blocks of material that can be described by a fixed shape, they can either be considered StockMaterial or remain isotropic_material if they are not going to be combined with other StockMaterial to produce a composite part. The latter could take on the part types of extrusion, plate, bar, casting, forging, and tubing. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; Resins, stabilizers, foaming and film adhesives are types of isotropic_material. Also metals in general can be considered isotropic_material.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>isotropic_material</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_236160_29438" xmi:uuid="192f1901-9457-4329-ac38-98c1cae1ba39" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456300376191_614594_42940" xmi:uuid="dc55ca12-762b-48f9-acb9-a63d918eec24" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194163_236160_29438"/>
          <body> a stock_core is a type of StockMaterial that is processed to be placed within a laminate and play a role in enhancing the stiffness of the laminate. &lt;example&gt; Honeycomb, phenolic block, and corrugation are types of stock_core.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>stock_core</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194164_648808_29439" xmi:uuid="394804c3-ece2-47ce-bdc0-1190942f3bf1" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456300455421_323825_42941" xmi:uuid="244fdbc8-22a6-462d-ac1a-f098e76aa959" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194164_648808_29439"/>
          <body> a woven_assembly is a type of StockMaterial.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>woven_assembly</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
    </packagedElement>
