    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193104_250790_23577" xmi:uuid="bf91750f-98dc-4635-bb5e-76ca4f94f1ed" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_2aed05bf_1510766276920_487197_33712" xmi:uuid="10ef20d4-b289-4bda-8bc5-4991f156f70e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <body>Is Filament assembly material a filament laminate as well and not a filament assembly instead.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454499005988_899571_43229" xmi:uuid="a800d117-6140-45b5-a46f-b7a7757efdf2" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193104_250790_23577"/>
        <body>A FilamentLaminate is a type of ConstituentPart that is a bonded material of two or more bundles of filament construction. The FilamentLaminate defines a volume to fill with filament assemblies. &lt;note&gt; The shape of a FilamentLaminate may be defined by a cross section and a length. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; When a FilamentLaminate is made from a StockMaterial, it usually refers to individual tows, yarns, and rovings. These volumes can be as simple as the cross section and length of a radius filler to as complex as a filament wound vessel. FilamentLaminates that are made by pulling and forming processes, called pultrusions, may use a tape form of FilamentAssembly. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The difference between a ply and a FilamentLaminate, when referencing a StockMaterial, is that a ply describes a constant thickness area to be filled by a StockMaterial and a FilamentLaminate describes a general volume to be filled by a StockMaterial. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt;Pultruded shapes, radius fillers, and filament wound structure are types of FilamentLaminate (see following figure). &lt;/example&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;FilamentLaminate.png&lt;/name&gt;Filament laminate&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>FilamentLaminate</name>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1459328383656_343264_42567" xmi:uuid="9c22daea-0c01-4218-be99-624e1bbea167" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1714997368185_942202_151614" xmi:uuid="0733a2a3-8ee1-46e0-b374-c1fb656e7025" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1714997368185_57697_151615" xmi:uuid="e9a70d2d-4708-4c45-b8f6-cb911e6e16ed" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>&lt;sch:rule context="//PartView[@uid and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='FilamentLaminate' ]"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="stockMaterialRef" value="MadeFrom/@uidRef"&gt;&lt;/sch:let&gt; &lt;sch:assert test="//*[@uid=$stockMaterialRef]/StockMaterialType eq 'filament_assembly'"&gt;(FilamentLaminate.WR1 &lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt;) the stock material shall be of type filament assembly.&lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1459328425973_868191_42569" xmi:uuid="a2f5e4e3-8f5d-4d1e-9a77-fa811b25fd22" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1459328383656_343264_42567"/>
          <body> the stock material shall be of type filament assembly.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1671446868885_551611_162955" xmi:uuid="f0bb36f8-fd2a-4539-a5c8-1cc487328eba" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1671446874487_815668_162958" xmi:uuid="733bf118-ce38-43be-ba82-8493878d3634" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>WR1 : SELF.MadeFrom.StockMaterialType = filament_assembly;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>EXPRESS</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR1</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193104_250790_23577"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1509035790846_125263_30498" xmi:uuid="8c9d991b-5187-482d-8959-55df00dc9a8a" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>self.MadeFrom.StockMaterialType = Application_protocols::AP242::Domain_model::CompositeStructuralShapeAndStructure::StockCategoryEnum::filament_assembly</body>
          <language>OCL2.0</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193541_857114_25826" xmi:uuid="284043b5-402c-406a-b67d-31e04ded72d8" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193055_357027_23478"/>
      </generalization>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193513_987077_25560" xmi:uuid="33e5a4e9-cc11-4cf9-9a5d-bd632ce52e15" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193045_539261_23454"/>
      </generalization>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193691_22800_26938" xmi:uuid="c0ee969a-78ea-482f-9297-f5d22d7380b4" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193267_645364_23876"/>
      </generalization>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193691_563405_26940" xmi:uuid="30cbb2c9-f877-4462-aaed-e17f0e1624d6" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454499112484_691863_43230" xmi:uuid="2d3fce30-9c5a-44f4-8655-8308ff4c8f77" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193691_563405_26940"/>
          <body> specifies the stock StockMaterial that the FilamentLaminate is made from. The FilamentLaminate is in the form of a tow, yarn or roving, and sometimes tape.</body>
        </ownedComment>
