    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193182_482060_23739" xmi:uuid="c687d7a0-7891-44c8-a34f-8714b322515c" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454499637385_832893_43259" xmi:uuid="d829c2af-128e-43c6-9ff8-b52ecf64cfa7" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193182_482060_23739"/>
        <body>A PlyLaminate is a type of ConstituentPart that is formed by two or more Ply objects that mate with each other. The plies have unique orientation and shape within the PlyLaminate. &lt;note&gt;Examples of PlyLaminate shape include angle, cap, flat, general contour, simple contour, complex contour, channel, etc. (see following figure). &lt;/note&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;PlyLaminate.png&lt;/name&gt;Ply laminate&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>PlyLaminate</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193541_628431_25828" xmi:uuid="50ac5d6e-b766-4241-b965-775580eeb90e" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
